# Line endings are LF in the working tree on every platform, not only in the object store.
#
# This is not tidiness. Since `I-01` the manifest records the byte size and the SHA-256 of every
# published file, and the Angular builder copies `src/assets` into `dist` verbatim — so with the
# default Windows checkout the same commit produces a different manifest on a developer's machine
# than in CI (sills.json: 4 325 bytes against 4 149, and a different hash on every text asset).
# The regenerate-and-diff gate would fail for the platform rather than for the data, and the
# checksums would describe bytes nobody is served.
#
# Git already stores LF; this only stops the checkout from converting it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never converted or diffed.
*.bin.gz binary
*.gz binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.svg text eol=lf
